WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.420
Welcome to Configuration Management. In this lesson, we explore this purpose: Maintain the integrity and traceability of controlled work products.

2
00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:19.960
Consider this scenario. An unapproved library version reaches production. First understand the problem before producing documentation.

3
00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:30.400
Start with two steps: Identify controlled items and owners. Then Establish reviewed baselines. Each step should be explained and evidenced.

4
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:40.370
Continue with Authorize and trace change requests. Then Audit delivered configurations. Verify the results against the intended outcome.

5
00:00:40.370 --> 00:01:01.780
Stronger evidence looks like this: Stronger: contemporaneous baseline register, approved change records, configuration audit tied to real work. Weaker evidence would be: Weaker: assuming a Git repository alone guarantees configuration integrity; no trace of consistent use. Triangulate independent sources.

6
00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:16.030
Now your turn. Review four documents and two interviews, identify inconsistencies and complete the mastery challenge. This video is an independent teaching explanation, not official CMMI model wording.
